WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.470
Welcome to your second drink of Weight Loss Part 2.
欢迎收看《减肥》第二部分内容的第二杯饮品。

2
00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.970
Jenna, you had a soapbox in this episode.
珍娜，你在这一集里发表了一番慷慨激昂的见解。

3
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.530
We got this letter from Tara M.
我们收到了塔拉·M发来的这封信。

4
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:17.390
Jenna, I just wanted you to know that I was so with you today on Part 2
珍娜，我只是想让你知道，今天在第二部分里，我太赞同你了

5
00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.950
when you talked about all the hate Pam gets.
当你在谈论潘所受到的所有恶意时。

6
00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.990
It's absolutely 100% sexism.
这绝对是百分之百的性别歧视。

7
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.930
Thank you so much for saying so.
非常感谢你这么说。

8
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.230
I support you and love you both so much.
我非常支持你们两个，也很爱你们。

9
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:28.910
Well, thank you, Tara.
好的，谢谢你，塔拉。

10
00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:35.930
I am aware that my soapbox from this episode created a lot of debate
我很清楚我在这一集里的慷慨陈词引发了大量的讨论

11
00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.170
of people arguing back and forth.
人们在争论不休。

12
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.270
But I think I helped some people see things in a new way.
但我认为我帮助一些人以崭新的视角看待问题。

13
00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:44.710
And now, you know, 15 years later,
而且现在，你知道的，15年过去了，

14
00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:48.350
people are really seeing the Jim Pam situation a little differently.
人们对吉姆和潘的情况确实有了些许不同的看法。

15
00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:53.170
You know, some of the things that were seen as romantic 15 years ago,
你知道的，15年前被视为浪漫的一些事情，

16
00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:55.510
they hit a little different now.
现在感觉有点不太一样了。

17
00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:00.650
Like, maybe it's not so romantic to surprise your wife by buying a house.
比如，给妻子一个惊喜，买下一栋房子，也许并不是那么浪漫。

18
00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:06.650
Maybe it's not neat to invest your savings and take a job out of town
也许把积蓄投进去，在另一个城市的一家创业公司找一份工作，却不告诉她，这并不是一件很酷的事，当你们还有两个年幼的孩子

19
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:10.810
at a startup without telling her when you have two small kids
而照顾孩子的重担全都要落到她一个人头上时。

20
00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:13.050
whose care is all going to fall to her.
当你把这些大声说出来时，就会觉得，什么？

21
00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:16.130
When you say that out loud, that's like, what?
你动用了我们的积蓄？

22
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.570
You took our savings?
你在外地找了工作？

23
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.330
You got a job out of town?
就像，我们没有商量过吗？

24
00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.070
Like, we didn't talk this out?
而且还是去一家靠不住的创业公司。

25
00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:22.290
With like an insecure startup.
是的。

26
00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:22.750
Yeah.
而且他好几个星期都不告诉她。

27
00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.930
And he doesn't tell her for weeks.
我知道。

28
00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:25.430
I know.
这就好比达里尔不得不说服他，

29
00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.130
It's like Daryl has to convince him to be like,
你打算告诉潘吗？

30
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.350
are you going to tell Pam?
就像，我们很快就要去费城了。

31
00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:32.070
Like, we're leaving for Philly soon.
就像，你打算什么时候让她知道这一切？

32
00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:34.110
Like, when are you going to bring her in the loop?
所以我认为，现在观看《办公室》的年轻一代

33
00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.970
So I think it's hitting a little differently now
对这一集的看法有些不同了。

34
00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.550
with this younger generation that's watching The Office.
那些观众会觉得，

35
00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.570
And those folks are like,
我觉得潘有点脾气也许是对的。

36
00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:44.870
I think maybe Pam's right to be a little grumpy.
是的。

37
00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:45.390
Yeah.
比如，对伴侣做出的某事感到恼火，并不是不支持对方。

38
00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:49.990
Like, it's not unsupportive to be annoyed that your partner did something.
但是，当这一集刚播出时，我因此挨了很多骂。

39
00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.790
But yeah, when the episode first aired, I got a lot of shit for it.
这也让我想起，我最近重温了《绝命毒师》。

40
00:01:55.890 --> 00:02:00.510
And it reminds me, too, I recently did a rewatch of Breaking Bad.
你还记得《绝命毒师》刚上映的时候吗？

41
00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:03.490
Do you remember when Breaking Bad first came out?
安娜·冈，饰演斯凯勒·怀特的演员，

42
00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:07.250
Anna Gunn, the actress who played Skylar White,
也就是沃尔特·怀特的妻子。

43
00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:10.050
you know, married to Walter White.
她因为对丈夫变成一个冰毒大亨

44
00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:17.330
She got a lot of shit for, like, how hurt and upset she was
感到受伤和心烦意乱而受到了很多恶评。

45
00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:22.030
that her husband was becoming a methamphetamine drug kingpin.
她的心里实在容不下这个。

46
00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:24.090
She didn't have space in her heart for that.
而且这很有趣，因为当我重温时，

47
00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:28.830
Like, and it's interesting because when I rewatched it,
我想，天哪。

48
00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.690
I was like, oh, my God.
我觉得她的表演简直太精湛了。

49
00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:36.770
She was, like, I thought her performance is just, like, spot on.
你能想象吗？

50
00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:37.730
Could you imagine?
你能想象吗？

51
00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:39.050
Could you imagine?
你能想象吗？

52
00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:42.950
But everybody was so dazzled by the charismatic Walter White.
但大家都为充满魅力的沃尔特·怀特所倾倒。

53
00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:44.870
They were pissed that she wasn't more supportive.
他们很不高兴她不够支持他。

54
00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.450
That's so wild.
真是太疯狂了。

55
00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:50.010
Okay, so I also talked about an amazing deleted scene
好的，我还谈到了一场精彩的删减片段

56
00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.510
with Ryan getting yelled at by David Wallace.
讲的是瑞安被大卫·华莱士大声斥责。

57
00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:56.530
David is so mad when he calls and Ryan answers the phone.
大卫打电话来时气极了，而接电话的是瑞安。

58
00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.690
You know, Ryan was stealing from the company.
你知道的，瑞安当时在偷公司的东西。

59
00:02:58.930 --> 00:02:59.770
What the hell?
搞什么鬼？

60
00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:01.130
Now he's answering the phones again?
现在他又开始接电话了？

61
00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:04.610
There's this great scene with Michael on the phone with David.
有一个很棒的场景是迈克尔和大卫通电话。

62
00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.610
And I brought it up in our breakdown.
我在我们的解析中提到了这一点。

63
00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.750
It's been added back to the superfan episode.
它已经被加回到超级粉丝版剧集里了。

64
00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.350
And I just wanted everyone to hear it.
我只是想让大家听听这个。

65
00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:11.330
I want him.
我想要他。

66
00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:15.330
Allegedly.
据称。

67
00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:15.810
No.
不。

68
00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:20.820
Allegedly admitted his guilt.
据称承认了他的罪行。

69
00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:21.960
What?
什么？

70
00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.140
Listen, David.
听着，大卫。

71
00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:25.200
I.
我。

72
00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:25.820
Michael.
迈克尔。

73
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:26.840
I know Ryan.
我了解瑞安。

74
00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:27.740
Michael.
迈克尔。

75
00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:28.880
He is good people.
他是个好人。

76
00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:30.800
He made a huge, huge error.
他犯了一个极其严重的错误。

77
00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.460
I just, I think he needs direction.
我只是，我觉得他需要方向。

78
00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.100
That's all.
就这样。

79
00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:35.540
Fuck.
他妈的。

80
00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.480
I'm tired, Michael.
我很累，迈克尔。

81
00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:37.100
Me too.
我也是。

82
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:37.840
Okay.
好吧。

83
00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.890
You really want to go out on for this?
你真的要为这事跟我杠到底吗？

84
00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:43.110
With all my heart.
我全心全意。

85
00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:43.510
Yes.
是的。

86
00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:44.470
Fine.
好吧。

87
00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:45.690
He can't talk to.
他不能跟……讲话。

88
00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:51.760
Woo.
呜。

89
00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:52.660
On me.
算在我的头上。

90
00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.160
What do I have to do with it?
这跟我有什么关系？

91
00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:55.060
Michael.
迈克尔。

92
00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.320
I mean, this guy has a criminal record.
我的意思是，这家伙有犯罪记录。

93
00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:57.480
I think that's a little excessive.
我觉得这有点过分了。

94
00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:01.200
Whoa.
哇。

95
00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:01.560
Wait.
等等。

96
00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:02.340
On me?
算在我的头上？

97
00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:03.960
Yes, Michael.
是的，迈克尔。

98
00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.600
You brought him back.
是你把他带回来的。

99
00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:06.860
Amazing.
太惊艳了。

100
00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:07.800
It's so good.
太棒了。

101
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.060
And Andy Buckley's so great in that scene.
而且安迪·巴克利在那场戏里演得太棒了。

102
00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.640
Well, listen, I have one last letter to share.
听着，我还有最后一封信要分享。

103
00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:13.700
It's from Megan M.
它来自梅根·M。

104
00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:14.360
Who says,
信上说：

105
00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:18.120
Hey, I found a little error in the last Office Ladies episode.
嘿，我在上一期《办公室女士》里发现了一个小错误。

106
00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:25.180
Jenna and Angela said that Kelly had the same nameplate that she was gifted in the Office Christmas Party episode.
珍娜和安吉拉说，凯莉桌上的名牌和她在《办公室圣诞派对》那一集里收到的礼物是同一个。

107
00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:27.660
But upon looking at it, it's a different plate.
但仔细一看，其实是不同的名牌。

108
00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:35.420
The one in the Christmas episode is purple with seven orange, blue, and pink stemless daisy-ish flowers.
圣诞那一集里的名牌是紫色的，上面有七朵橙色、蓝色和粉红色的无梗雏菊状花朵。

109
00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:39.160
But the plate on her desk in this episode is different.
但这集里她桌上的名牌却不一样。

110
00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:43.880
It's metallic, and there are only two red flowers with steMs.
它是金属质感的，而且只有两朵带茎的红花。

111
00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:50.060
So it's a floral plate, but not the same one that was gifted to her in Christmas Party.
所以这确实是个花卉名牌，但跟圣诞派对上送她的并不是同一个。

112
00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:50.840
Huh.
哈。

113
00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.180
Well, lady, you know what I did.
好吧，这位女士，你知道我干了什么。

114
00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.220
Asad basad.
太糟糕了。

115
00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.100
You know I did.
你知道我干了。

116
00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.120
Look, there it is.
看，就在那儿。

117
00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:57.020
It's different.
它是不一样的。

118
00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.480
Oh, my goodness.
噢，天哪。

119
00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.000
Megan, you're so right.
梅根，你太对了。

120
00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:00.800
Megan is right.
梅根是对的。

121
00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:05.120
Clearly, there is a theme here, and that is fancy font with flowers.
很显然，这里有一个共同的主题，那就是带花的艺术字体。

122
00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:05.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

123
00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:06.700
But they're totally different.
但它们完全不同。

124
00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:07.720
Totally different.
完全不同。

125
00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:14.420
And Megan, thank you for giving me the opportunity to do a side-by-side, which you know is one of my favorite things to do.
梅根，谢谢你给了我做对比图的机会，你知道这是我最喜欢做的事情之一。

126
00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:16.080
All right, you guys.
好了，各位。

127
00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.120
Here is your second drink of weight loss, part two.
这是你们的第二杯减肥饮料，第二部分。

128
00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.240
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

129
00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:25.540
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

130
00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:26.820
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

131
00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.080
And we're best friends.
我们是好朋友。

132
00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.900
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们专为你制作了《办公室终极重温》播客。

133
00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:38.880
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的两个人才能讲出的独家幕后故事。

134
00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.020
We're The Office ladies.
我们是办公室女士。

135
00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:44.460
Hey, gang.
嘿，各位。

136
00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:45.060
How's it going?
最近怎么样？

137
00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:46.240
Howdy.
大家好。

138
00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.860
It is Weight Loss Part 2.
这就是《减肥》第二部分。

139
00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:50.580
Season 5.
第五季。

140
00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:51.640
Yeah.
没错。

141
00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.940
This is the second part of our Season 5 premiere.
这是我们第五季首播集的第二部分。

142
00:05:55.220 --> 00:06:00.500
It was written by Lee Eisenberg and Gene Stepnitsky and directed by Paul Feig.
它由李·艾森伯格和吉恩·斯蒂普尼茨基编剧，保罗·费格执导。

143
00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:01.720
Hit us with a summary.
给我们来个总结吧。

144
00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:02.580
All right.
好的。

145
00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:08.840
Well, you might remember last week we set up that Dunder Mifflin is doing a company-wide weight loss conteSt.
大家可能还记得，上周我们提到邓德米夫林正在举办一场全公司范围的减肥比赛。

146
00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.960
That contest continues.
这场比赛仍在继续。

147
00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:13.720
It's really causing some division among the employees.
这确实在员工之间造成了一些分歧。

148
00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.120
People are getting hangry.
大家开始因为饥饿而脾气暴躁了。

149
00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:15.940
They are.
确实如此。

150
00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:18.520
Ryan returns to Scranton.
瑞安回到了斯克兰顿。

151
00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:19.880
He's a temp again.
他又成临时工了。

152
00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:25.120
Michael hires him to fill in at reception for Pam, who is off at Pratt.
迈克尔雇他来前台顶替去普瑞特艺术学院的帕姆。

153
00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.660
She's, you know, doing art school.
你知道的，她在上艺术学校。

154
00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:31.500
Now Michael is very slowly still pursuing Holly.
现在迈克尔依然在非常缓慢地追求霍莉。

155
00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:36.280
Dwight and Angela are continuing to hook up in the warehouse behind Andy's back.
德怀特和安吉拉瞒着安迪，继续在仓库里鬼混。

156
00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:39.560
And Jim has an important question for Pam.
而吉姆有一个重要问题要问帕姆。

157
00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:43.220
All right.
好的。

158
00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:44.820
Fast fact number one.
趣味冷知识第一条。

159
00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:51.680
Paul Feig directed this episode, and he also had a much larger role overall in Season 5.
保罗·费格执导了这一集，他在整个第五季中也担任了更重要的整体角色。

160
00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:56.940
Paul was with us for every single episode of Season 5.
保罗参与了第五季的每一集。

161
00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:57.960
He was.
确实如此。

162
00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.260
And he was amazing.
而且他太棒了。

163
00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:04.740
He was this great, constant, like, I don't know, Jen.
他就像是个伟大、稳定的人物，怎么说呢，珍。

164
00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.260
He was like the man of the ship.
他就像是这艘船的舵手。

165
00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.380
He was like guiding us along the way.
他一路上指引着我们。

166
00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.220
Having him on set always just made me feel better.
片场有他在总是让我感觉安心一些。

167
00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:12.320
I'm with you.
我赞同你。

168
00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:13.440
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

169
00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:21.900
You remember last week we talked about how Greg Daniels was now working on both The Office and he was trying to get Parks and Rec off the ground.
大家还记得上周我们聊过格雷格·丹尼尔斯当时既要制作《办公室》，又在筹备《公园与游憩》吗。

170
00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:26.940
He had groomed Jen Salata and Paul Lieberstein to run the show.
他培养了珍·萨拉塔和保罗·利伯斯坦来负责这部剧。

171
00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.500
They were overseeing the writing of the show.
他们负责监督本剧的编剧工作。

172
00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:30.960
They were running the writer's room.
他们管理着编剧室。

173
00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:42.200
Well, Paul Feig was brought on as a supervising director and co-executive producer to oversee the on-set production and to oversee all of our directors.
保罗·费格被请来担任总导演兼联合执行制片人，负责监督现场制作以及我们所有的导演。

174
00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:49.740
Because we had a lot of new directors in Season 5, including some cast members and crew members and even some of our writers.
因为我们在第五季有很多新导演，包括一些演员、剧组工作人员，甚至还有我们的编剧。

175
00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.880
They all directed their first episodes.
他们都执导了自己的第一集。

176
00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:59.440
Paul was also in the writer's room a bit, but mostly he was like the tastemaker, right?
保罗也稍微参与了编剧室的工作，但主要来说他就像是个风向标，对吧？

177
00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.660
He was like one of these original visionaries.
他就像是最初的富有远见者之一。

178
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.320
What is a tastemaker?
什么是风向标人物？

179
00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:11.440
I mean, I don't know, but I think a tastemaker is like you set the tastes of...
我的意思是，我不知道，但我认为风向标人物就像是你来引领……

180
00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.720
Did you make up that word?
这个词是你自己捏造的吧？

181
00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.740
No, tastemaker's a real word!
不对，风向标人物是个真正的词！

182
00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:19.160
Well, maybe if you're like running a winery.
好吧，也许你是在经营酒庄的话吧。

183
00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:24.500
But you can be like a tastemaker-like is the same as like a...
但你可以成为风向标人物，这就跟……

184
00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:25.960
I think you made it up.
我觉得这是你编出来的。

185
00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:26.900
Well, I didn't.
才没有。

186
00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:27.900
You can Google it.
你可以用谷歌搜一下。

187
00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.660
I can't believe you're getting out your phone right now to Google it.
我真不敢相信你现在居然掏出手机去谷歌。

188
00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.700
This is unbelievable.
这简直难以置信。

189
00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:35.520
Tastemaker is a real word.
风向标人物是个真词。

190
00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:36.640
It's like a trendsetter.
就像潮流引领者一样。

191
00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:37.460
Yes.
是的。

192
00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:38.420
Thank you, Sam.
谢谢你，萨姆。

193
00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:40.300
It's like a trendsetter.
就像潮流引领者一样。

194
00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:41.340
Okay?
好吗？

195
00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:42.500
Tastemaker.
风向标人物。

196
00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:42.940
Okay.
好吧。

197
00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:50.020
According to the English language learner's definition, a person whose judgment about what is good, fashionable, etc.
根据英语学习者词典的定义，一个对什么是好东西、时尚等有判断力的人……

198
00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:52.600
are accepted and followed by many other people.
其判断被许多其他人接受并追随。

199
00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:53.620
That's right.
没错。

200
00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.340
He was a tastemaker.
他就是个风向标人物。

201
00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:56.740
He was a tastemaker.
他是个潮流引领者。

202
00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:58.300
He was.
他的确是。

203
00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:01.380
It was his job to control the quality of the show.
他的工作就是把控节目的质量。

204
00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:06.480
You know, he said yes to jokes and no to other jokes because of his good taste.
你知道的，他凭着自己出色的审美品味，决定哪些笑话能用，哪些不能。

205
00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:07.320
I know.
我知道。

206
00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.460
This is getting us off so early.
我们这下开局大好。

207
00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.640
I really want to know the origin of this word.
我真的很想知道这个词的起源。

208
00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.160
Like, where did the word tastemaker come from?
比如说，“潮流引领者”这个词是从哪来的？

209
00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:19.160
Was that the person that, like, tried the food for the king and if he didn't die, okay, fine, we'll all eat what that guy had?
是不是那种帮国王试毒的人，如果他没死，行吧，那大家就都吃他吃过的东西？

210
00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:22.580
I don't know, but I think you should deep dive it for a revisited, Angela.
我不知道，但我觉得安吉拉，你应该好好深入研究一下，在节目重温时讲讲。

211
00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:22.850
Okay, fine.
好吧，行。

212
00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:23.600
I do.
我是这么想的。

213
00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:24.200
Okay.
好吧。

214
00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:25.800
Paul Feig was the tastemaker.
保罗·费格就是那个潮流引领者。

215
00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:26.500
Wow.
哇。

216
00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.440
You know what just happened there, Angela?
你知道刚刚发生什么了吗，安吉拉？

217
00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:29.080
What?
什么？

218
00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.940
You just got real hot and bothered with me.
你刚才对我有点激动和烦躁了。

219
00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:32.780
I did not.
我才没有。

220
00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:33.760
You did.
你有。

221
00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.420
That is not hot and bothered.
那不是激动和烦躁。

222
00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:38.000
That is perplexed and curious.
那是困惑和好奇。

223
00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.440
And you were right there.
而且你刚才就在那儿。

224
00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:41.000
You were real.
你真的……

225
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:41.640
You were right.
你猜对了。

226
00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.380
You were real hot to trot.
你当时真是急不可耐。

227
00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:47.620
That means wanting sex.
那意思是渴望性爱。

228
00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:49.120
I know what that means now.
我现在知道那是什么意思了。

229
00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:50.100
All right.
好吧。

230
00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:58.440
Well, listen, I talked to Greg Daniels about it, and he said that this was a big push that he had to make with the network.
总之，听着，我和格雷格·丹尼尔斯聊过这件事，他说这是他当时不得不向电视台极力争取的一点。

231
00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:07.200
In particular, Jerry DeCannio, the head of production at Universal, because our show had been functioning just fine without someone in this role before.
特别是环球影城的制作负责人杰里·德卡尼奥，因为在此之前，我们的节目一直没有设立这个职位也运转得很好。

232
00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:15.400
But Greg explained he was often called down to set to discuss the shooting or the motivations with the actors and directors,
但格雷格解释说，他过去经常被叫到片场去和演员、导演讨论拍摄或是动机问题，

233
00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:19.720
and he wanted to make sure that that would still be covered while he was gone.
他想确保他不在的时候这些工作也能兼顾到。

234
00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:25.640
And they eventually agreed, and I traded some messages with Paul Feig about this, too.
他们最终同意了，而且我也和保罗·费格就这事互发了一些消息。

235
00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.320
And he even sent in an audio clip.
他甚至还发来了一段音频。

236
00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.520
Ooh, Paul Feig!
哦，保罗·费格！

237
00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:31.840
All the way from London!
远从伦敦发来！

238
00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:32.400
Yep.
没错。

239
00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.780
It was such a fun year because, you know,
那真是非常开心的一年，因为你知道的，

240
00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:45.020
to be around you guys and the cast every day and to be in that writer's room with that amazing group of writers was just such a special opportunity.
每天能和你们大家以及演员们在一起，能和那群优秀的编剧一起待在编剧室里，真的是一次非常特别的机会。

241
00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:47.700
Yeah, I got to direct a lot of episodes that season,
对，那一季我执导了很多集，

242
00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:54.600
but also it was just fun to kind of be with all these other people who were starting to direct and seeing how great they were doing.
但同时，能和所有这些开始尝试导演工作的人在一起，看他们表现得那么棒，也真的很有趣。

243
00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:59.520
It was so fun to be with Steve when he directed his first episode, and Brent Forrester did a great job, and Dave Rogers.
能和史蒂夫在一起经历他执导第一集时真的很开心，布伦特·福雷斯特干得也很棒，还有戴夫·罗杰斯。

244
00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:06.080
We had so much fun, and so that was kind of my experience of the fifth season was being around everybody so much,
我们过得太开心了，所以第五季对我的体验来说，就是能和大家待在一起很长时间，

245
00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:16.420
but also just kind of getting to see the show through a lot of fresh eyes of these new directors or people coming out and doing it for the first time.
同时也通过这些新导演或初次执导的人的全新视角来欣赏这部剧。

246
00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:26.200
Well, I want to say that Paul also directed five episodes himself this season, and when we were trading messages, Angela,
嗯，我想说保罗这一季自己也执导了五集，而且安吉拉，在我们互发消息时，

247
00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:33.400
he said he loved his time on season five so much that he wanted to send us audio clips for every single episode of season five.
他说他太喜欢第五季的时光了，以至于想为第五季的每一集都给我们发一段音频。

248
00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:34.500
Get out!
少来这一套！

249
00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:35.400
Paulopedia!
保罗百科全书！

250
00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:36.920
Paulopedia!
保罗百科全书！

251
00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:40.040
I was like, Paul, you're busy.
我当时就说，保罗，你很忙。

252
00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:42.240
You're directing a movie right now in London.
你现在正在伦敦导一部电影。

253
00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.840
I mean, you don't have to do that.
我的意思是，你没必要这么做。

254
00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:45.560
And he said, well, I'll do as many as I can.
他说，好吧，我能拍多少就拍多少。

255
00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:46.840
So guys, get ready.
所以大家，准备好吧。

256
00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:50.140
Get ready for, should it be Figapedia or Paulopedia?
准备好迎接，究竟该叫菲加百科还是保罗百科？

257
00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:51.680
Paulfigapedia?
保罗菲加百科？

258
00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:52.680
Paulfigapedia!
保罗菲加百科！

259
00:11:56.380 --> 00:12:01.200
All right, fast fact number two is an art school location breakdown.
好的，快讯第二条是关于艺术学校的取景地解析。

260
00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:03.240
We didn't do this last week.
我们上周没讲这个。

261
00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:06.540
We're going to see more of art school this week, so I thought it was appropriate.
这周我们会看到更多关于艺校的内容，所以我觉得很合适。

262
00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:12.860
Fan question from Yvette and Rachel, where were the New York City art school scenes shot?
伊薇特和蕾切尔的粉丝提问，纽约艺术学校的场景是在哪里拍的？

263
00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:14.240
I will tell you.
我来告诉你们。

264
00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:18.880
Everything was shot at USC, the University of Southern California.
所有镜头都是在南加州大学（USC）拍的。

265
00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:24.040
The classrooms were empty classrooms on campus that our set decorators dressed.
教室是校园里空置的教室，由我们的布景师装扮的。

266
00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:27.380
Even the dorm room was a USC dorm room.
就连宿舍也是南加大的宿舍。

267
00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:33.000
The hallways, when Jim's watching TV in the common room, we were basically all on campus.
走廊，还有吉姆在公共休息室看电视的场景，我们基本上都在校园里。

268
00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:38.860
The only thing we didn't do on campus, and we talked about this last week, was when Jim and Pam are video chatting.
唯一不在校园里拍的，我们上周也讨论过了，就是吉姆和帕姆视频聊天的时候。

269
00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:42.600
They recreated my dorm room on that warehouse set of Dunder Mifflin.
他们在邓德米弗林的仓库片场重建了我的宿舍。

270
00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:48.660
Well, I have one other thing to share about the USC campus, but I am going to save it when it comes up in the episode.
好吧，关于南加大校园我还有另一件事要分享，但我要留到剧集里相关桥段出现时再说。

271
00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:49.760
Well, all right.
好吧，行。

272
00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:55.080
I have one fun thing to share about the real Pratt, which is in Brooklyn.
关于真正的普瑞特艺术学院，也就是位于布鲁克林的那个，我有一个趣事要分享。

273
00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.080
That's where Pam's meant to be.
那是帕姆应该去的地方。

274
00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.980
There's a communal cat population living on campus called Pratt cats.
校园里生活着一群被称为普瑞特猫的流浪猫社群。

275
00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:10.960
They have their own little houses, and they wander the lecture halls and the campus freely.
它们有自己的小房子，在阶梯教室和校园里自由闲逛。

276
00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:17.740
If you're ever in New York, I highly recommend you visit the campus, along with its sculptures and cats roaming the grounds.
如果你去纽约，我强烈建议你去参观一下校园，还有那里漫步的雕塑和猫咪。

277
00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:24.160
Angela, the cats even have their own Instagram page, and it's called Pratt cats.
安吉拉，这些猫甚至有它们自己的Instagram主页，就叫普瑞特猫。

278
00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:25.400
Pratt cats?
普瑞特猫？

279
00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:26.540
That's so cute.
太可爱了。

280
00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:29.520
Two T's for Pratt and two T's for cats.
普瑞特的Pratt有两个t，猫的cats也有两个t。

281
00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:30.660
Pratt cats.
普瑞特猫。

282
00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:31.460
Pratt cats.
普瑞特猫。

283
00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:32.580
I looked at it.
我看过了。

284
00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:34.680
It's just a lot of super cute pictures of cats.
里面全是超可爱的猫咪照片。

285
00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:35.980
I want to see it.
我想看。

286
00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:39.220
Oh my gosh, there's so many.
哦天哪，有这么多。

287
00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:40.060
Yeah.
是啊。

288
00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:41.720
I wonder who does the Instagram.
我不知道是谁在运营这个Instagram。

289
00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.140
There's so many cats.
有好多猫。

290
00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.200
I think we should put this on our liSt.
我觉得我们应该把它列入清单。

291
00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:46.360
We should.
我们应该这么做。

292
00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:47.660
All right.
好了。

293
00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.000
Fast fact number three.
快讯第三条。

294
00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:51.280
We've got a big guest star alert.
我们迎来了大牌客串明星警报。

295
00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:55.500
It's Rich Summer as Pam's art school friend, Alex.
里奇·萨默饰演帕姆的艺校朋友亚历克斯。

296
00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.640
Yes, and we are friends with Rich.
没错，而且我们和里奇是好朋友。

297
00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.800
We're like really good friends with Rich.
我们跟里奇关系真的非常好。

298
00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:01.980
He needs to come on.
他得来上节目。

299
00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:03.060
Well, he's refused.
嗯，他拒绝了。

300
00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:04.460
No, he has not.
不对，他才没有。

301
00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:07.280
We are going to have him on.
我们将邀请他做客节目。

302
00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:18.120
You guys, Rich is probably most well-known for his role as Harry Crane on Mad Men, but he's also acted in such shows as Wet Hot American Summer, the TV series,
伙计们，里奇最著名的角色大概是《广告狂人》里的哈里·克兰，但他也参演过诸如《湿热的美利坚夏天》电视剧版，

303
00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:21.960
as well as many movies with Office Connections.
以及许多与《办公室》有关的电影。

304
00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:22.460
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

305
00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:25.580
He was in The Devil Wears Prada, starring Emily Blunt.
他出演过由艾米莉·布朗特主演的《穿普拉达的女王》。

306
00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:29.320
He was in Celeste and Jessie Forever, starring Rashida Jones.
他出演过由拉什达·琼斯主演的《离婚不分手》。

307
00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:33.080
And he was in The Giant Mechanical Man, starring me.
他还出演过由我主演的《巨型机械人》。

308
00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:33.760
Yay!
太棒了！

